From 9d97b4b003661ad4832fe703dc5649ca807739ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:47:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Docs: custody v2 - who holds x in the single-seat bootstrap;
 goals are targets, admin and business controls kept

Prose only (root doc-accuracy review); no code, contract or site-bundle change (docs/ is not in the site build).
- 4.1: with t = 1 (genesis and production today) the one share is x itself; the full committee scalar exists inside
  the single Enclave seat's SEV-SNP custodian guest, sealed, never host plaintext. Threshold distribution starts only
  after a multi-seat handover, and below 3 seats the Enclave seat can still reconstruct x (6.2).
- 2: the goals are multi-seat design targets, not the current single-seat state; they do not remove Enclave's
  administrative and business controls (the EnclaveAddressBook administrator still chooses secretVaultV2 and
  sessionVaultFactory).
- 9: "Gives" is scoped to committees with n >= 3 seats.
The dated 2026-10-14 deployment table and the 2026-10-23 current-state section are unchanged.
---
 docs/security/secret-custody-v2.md | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

